  "prompt": [
    "Client: Harbourline Commerce, a multi-tenant retail order platform with about 400 tenants. Database hlc-orders-prod: Azure SQL Database, Business Critical, Gen5, 16 vCores, compatibility level 160, READ_COMMITTED_SNAPSHOT ON. All times are UTC. Business hours are 07:30 to 18:00. The nightly batch must finish by 06:00. Evidence was collected from Mon 21 Sep to Sun 27 Sep 2026.",
    "The CTO writes: 'Thursday got better after Azure moved us to a new node at 11:47. Microsoft obviously had a hardware",
    "problem.' The application logged 212 errors 40613 and 37 errors 49918 on Thu 24, all between 11:47:05 and 11:48:20,",
    "and every one of those requests succeeded on retry. Name why Thursday improved.",
    "Client change log: 2025-03-11 a developer added OPTION (MAX_GRANT_PERCENT = 5) to etl.LoadFactSales, then a daytime job. 2026-01-20 etl.LoadFactSales moved into the nightly pipeline. 2026-08-30 release 5.2: ORM upgrade from version 7 to 8, new ProductSearch endpoint. 2026-09-01 tenant 'MegaMart' onboarded; nightly volume about doubled. 2026-09-04 the nightly index job was changed: rebuild threshold 30% to 5%, reorganize removed, ONLINE = ON, MAXDOP = 0, and UPDATE STATISTICS WITH FULLSCAN on every user table added. 2026-09-16 hotfix 5.2.3: an outer retry policy on every database call and Max Pool Size 100 to 400. 2026-09-24 11:47 planned maintenance reconfiguration, completed 11:48."
  ],
